cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Multimodal Avocado Ripeness Research Program
message: >-
  If you use this proposal, its code or its derived data, please cite it as
  below, and cite the underlying Mendeley dataset separately (see NOTICE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arshyia
    family-names: Mehran
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-7960-2536
    affiliation: University of British Columbia
repository-code: https://github.com/Arshyi/AvocadoRipenessResearch
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22888386
abstract: >-
  An evidence-audited research proposal for non-destructive Hass avocado
  ripeness and remaining-useful-life estimation, released together with
  reproducible computational baselines. Includes a dataset rights audit,
  fruit-grouped machine-learning baselines with leakage controls and bootstrap
  confidence intervals, storage-condition stress tests, candidate kinetic
  models, a prototype architecture with an audited bill of materials, and a
  statistical plan. Results are an internal benchmark on one public CC BY 4.0
  dataset and are not a deployment claim. Not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - avocado
  - fruit ripeness
  - non-destructive sensing
  - machine learning
  - reproducibility
  - research proposal
